/// known-gap: interp scales a link into 0..1 over a range it guesses from the formula, and takes variable names
/// A link is declared with its range. `:link_score(a, b, "border")` is a's
/// link to b: its formula, plus the changes made to the pair, kept inside
/// the range. Links go one way: b's link to a is its own.
<>Nation |
    military: .5
    economy: .5
xx
link Nation border 0...1 by [
    self >> military * .5 + target >> economy * .25
]
link Nation respect -10...10
a <> Nation | military: .8, economy: .2
b <> Nation | military: .4, economy: .4
say(:link_score(a, b, "border"))
say(:link_score(b, a, "border"))
say(:link_score(a, b, "respect"))
a link to b on respect offset +4
say(:link_score(a, b, "respect"))
say(:link_score(b, a, "respect"))
a link to b on border offset +.9
say(:link_score(a, b, "border"))
